Fixes unsoundness in `--modular-termination` (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/211): a `decreases {:global}` or `decreases {:callback g}` bound could call code that reaches a call dispatched to implementations in other modules, such as a rank computed through dispatch, and then the checks of the bounds could use the definition of the very function whose termination they establish.  A program could so verify `assert false` and, when run, recurse forever.  Such a bound is now rejected, and the error names the route by which it reaches the dispatched call.
